# Line endings for generated artifacts.
#
# check_exports_current.py rebuilds every export into a temp dir and compares it
# byte for byte against what is committed. That comparison is only meaningful if
# a checkout produces the same bytes as a rebuild on EVERY platform. Without the
# rules below it did not, and the failure was invisible from Windows:
#
#   csv.DictWriter writes CRLF always (RFC 4180, not a platform default).
#   With no attribute set, autocrlf gave a Windows checkout CRLF -- match -- and
#   a Linux checkout LF -- mismatch on the first byte of every line. Every CSV
#   read STALE in CI and current locally, for eleven consecutive red runs.
#
# So: pin CSV to the CRLF its writer emits, and pin the text this pipeline
# generates to the LF that _common.atomic_write_text now writes everywhere.
# Repo blobs stay LF either way; this governs the working tree.

*.csv text eol=crlf
*.md  text eol=lf
